Add a ROM-level heartbeat probe just before nx_start() to pinpoint the
silent-boot stop.

The board boots the bootloader fine (markers @A..@E via ROM ets_printf reach
the USB-Serial/JTAG console), then goes completely silent -- no kernel or app
output at all, and the board does NOT reboot (300 s USB re-enumeration watch =
0 flaps).  Two hypotheses:
  (H1) the kernel hangs inside __esp32s3_start AFTER the @E marker (clock /
       RTC / esp32s3_board_initialize) or inside nx_start() early; or
  (H2) the kernel + app run, but NuttX's esp32s3 USBSERIAL *driver* TX is dead
       while the ROM ets_printf channel works -> every syslog/printf is dropped.

@F is a ROM ets_printf placed immediately before nx_start(); it prints even if
H2 is true.  The app entry marker lives in apps/examples/desktop_companion/
main.c (edited directly in staging, not via this nuttx patch) for the same
reason.  If @F prints but the app's [APP] marker does not -> kernel reached
nx_start but the init task never started (H1b).  If both print but the app's
own syslog(LOG_INFO) still does not -> H2 confirmed (NuttX USBSERIAL TX dead).

diff --git a/arch/xtensa/src/esp32s3/esp32s3_start.c b/arch/xtensa/src/esp32s3/esp32s3_start.c
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/arch/xtensa/src/esp32s3/esp32s3_start.c
+++ b/arch/xtensa/src/esp32s3/esp32s3_start.c
@@ -437,4 +437,5 @@
   /* Bring up NuttX */
 
+  ets_printf("[HB] @F nx_start entering\n");
   nx_start();
   for (; ; ); /* Should not return */
